# The WAL's cold load of an unloaded generation entry ignores the initiator's routing
# floor (#5697 review, S1). A cross-shard straddler: shard root s2 of the purged
# incarnation admitted a write whose keys, under the re-created tree's shard map,
# belong to L. L's first initialisation claims only its own shard root's generation,
# not s2's, and s2's re-created counterpart has not initialised. With s2's entry
# retired, only the WAL-side floor in the load refuses the write; without it, the write
# is allocated above L's recorded close. Moved from the design's
# ReadPositionHonestRoutingWalIgnoresFloor; under #5833's C1 the floor is read by the
# cold load rather than checked at a claim.
MODULE: StraddlerBelowInitRoutingWalIgnoresFloor
TARGET: StraddlerBelowInit
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the WAL's cold load ignores the initiator's routing floor
PERTURBS: ColdLoadApply

--- FIND
    /\ loaded' = [loaded EXCEPT ![i] = Max2(@, Max2(rd[i], walFloor[i]))]
    /\ fo' = [fo EXCEPT ![i] = IF loaded[i] = Unloaded THEN rd[i] <= walFloor[i] ELSE @]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the WAL-side floor is not taken.
    /\ loaded' = [loaded EXCEPT ![i] = Max2(@, rd[i])]
    /\ UNCHANGED fo
--- END
